While concurrent work evaluates VLA instruction following behaviorally~\cite{fang2026when,swann2026}, we provide complementary representational analysis of how instruction information is routed internally.
We ask: \emph{which representational changes are associated with VLA fine-tuning, and which are inherited from the pretrained backbone?}
Our contributions are:

tool_args.old_string:
\caption{\textbf{Action-relevant representations differ between trained and reference VLAs in a pattern specific to VLM-to-VLA transitions.}
VLM-to-VLA fine-tuning is associated with substantial $R^2$ exit collapse ($\Delta R^2 > 0.10$), whereas VLA-to-VLA fine-tuning shows only small fluctuations.
L1 instruction attention reflects inherited base-model priors, not VLA training.}

